README.md (inside /atmosphere)
Atmosphere — Independent Audit Universe

Atmosphere is a parallel, independent audit layer that exists outside the ROOT system.
It does not participate in operational processes — it only observes, withdraws the status and saves the results in its own, isolated archive.

ROOT cannot write to Atmosphere.
Atmosphere cannot write to ROOT.
The link is one-way: read‑only simlink.
🌫️ What Atmosphere does

Atmosphere periodically wakes up (cron) and executes: 

read‑only log‑pull from ROOT 

SnapshotOps — capturing the current state 

IntegrityOps — structural and stability check 

DiffOps — a comparison with the previous state 

TimelineOps — tracking system evolution 

AnomalyOps — detection of unusual changes 

log‑drop — saving the results to your own archive

Atmosphere is a passive surveillance universe.
ROOT is just a data source.
🜁 Why it exists

The goal of the Atmosphere layer is to:

create a truth layer outside the operating system

provide objective auditing

have an independent archive that cannot be modified by ROOT

detect anomalies and unexpected changes

provide a security audit that is indestructible from the ROOT perspective



Architecture


ATMOSPHERE
 ├── CronWake
 ├── PullOps
 ├── RevisionLayer
 │     ├── SnapshotOps
 │     ├── IntegrityOps
 │     ├── DiffOps
 │     ├── TimelineOps
 │     └── AnomalyOps
 └── AuditArchive
       ├── log-drop
       ├── snapshots
       ├── diffs
       ├── timeline
       └── anomalies


Root

ROOT
 └── audit-symlink → ATMOSPHERE/AuditArchive

